,title,link,text,language,family
0,"Ewe language - Simple English Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia",https://simple.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ewe_language,"Ewe (Eʋe or Eʋegbe) is a language spoken by about 5 million people in West Africa, mainly in Ghana and Togo. Ewe is part of the Gbe languages. The other major Gbe language is Fon, which is mainly spoken in Benin.",Kpessi,Niger-Congo
1,"Kpessi Language (KEF) – L1 & L2 Speakers, Status... | Ethnologue Free",https://www.ethnologue.com/language/kef/,Kpessi is a stable indigenous language of Togo. It belongs to the Niger-Congo language family. The language is used as a first language by all in the ethnic community. It is not known to be taught in schools.,Kpessi,Niger-Congo
