3,Kpessi - kef (Niger-Congo) - PeopleGroups.org,https://peoplegroups.org/language/kef/,"Kpessi (kef) is part of the Niger-Congo family and Niger-Congo, Atlantic-Congo, Volta-Congo, Kwa, Left Bank, Gbe class.People Groups who primarily speak Kpessi. To download a comprehensive people group list in spreadsheet form, visit our Research Data page.",Kpessi,Niger-Congo
4,Kpessi,https://docs.verbix.com/EndangeredLanguages/Kpessi,"Language family: Niger-Congo, Atlantic-Congo, Volta-Congo, Kwa, Left Bank, Gbe (SIL classification). Number of speakers: 2,358-3,100.Traditional religion. Kpessi is spoken in Togo, Africa. Support the free Verbix verb conjugation services.",Kpessi,Niger-Congo
5,Kpessi in Togo people group profile | Joshua Project,https://joshuaproject.net/people_groups/12830/TO,"Learn about the Kpessi in Togo people group. Profiles include statistics, text, photo, map, progress indicator and language resources.Submit a profile. Scripture Prayers for the Kpessi in Togo.",Kpessi,Niger-Congo
6,What Languages do People Speak in Nigeria?,https://worldpopulationreview.com/countries/nigeria/language,"It is from the Niger-Congo language family and has as many as 24 million native speakers, both within and outside of Nigeria. There are over 20 dialects of Igbo, but Umuahia and Owerri are considered to be the official dialects.",Kpessi,Niger-Congo
